From 4ff8be9a36031e86704b562fabc16714f8c33421 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian Delwiche <delwiche@google.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 20:43:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] Fix SDP server heap buffer overflow

This change addresses a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the SDP
server where an oversized attribute could be serialized into a fixed
400-byte allocation during partial attribute responses.

To prevent out-of-bounds writes and subsequent out-of-bounds reads, this
commit enforces strict bounds checks against SDP_MAX_ATTR_LEN across
three areas:
1. Sizing the allocation dynamically in
sdpu_build_partial_attrib_entry
   and validating attribute bounds before serialization.
2. Adding explicit length checks to L2CAP continuation request branches
   in process_service_attr_req and process_service_search_attr_req.
3. Enforcing maximum attribute length limits during database insertion
   in sdp_add_attribute_to_record.

Also corrects a couple of mistaken bounds checks elsewhere in
sdp_server.cc.

Bug: 503554490
Test: atest net_test_stack_sdp
Flag: EXEMPT CVE_FIX
Change-Id: I3005192b7deb0ce2e259c9abac0077c00a9ebac0
---
